OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES COut with the revolving cube
OL,4,Cand in with the cylinder
OL,5,
OL,6,FARCHIVE: The TV Room
OL,7,
OL,8,F28th December marked the 50th
OL,9,Fanniversary of what is arguably the
OL,10,Fmost iconic version of BBC One's mirror
OL,11,Fglobe.
OL,12,
OL,13,FBut 28th December 1974 is also thought
OL,14,Fto be the date BBC Two got a refresh
OL,15,Ftoo.
OL,16,
OL,17,FThe revolving cube  '2' ident was
OL,18,Freplaced by the cylindrical lined '2'
OL,19,Fwhich remained in use until 1979.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G2/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES COut with the revolving cube
OL,4,Cand in with the cylinder
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe word "colour" did not feature on
OL,7,Fthe new ident ` just as it was
OL,8,Fwithdrawn from use on BBC One.
OL,9,
OL,10,FThis reflected a conscious decision by
OL,11,FBBC TV ` or at least Presentation ` to
OL,12,Fstop actively promoting the fact an
OL,13,Findividual programme was in colour.
OL,14,
OL,15,FBy then, all new network programmes and
OL,16,Froutine repeats of programmes less than
OL,17,Ftwo years old were in colour.
OL,18,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13103
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G3/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES COut with the revolving cube
OL,4,Cand in with the cylinder
OL,5,
OL,6,FOther than the Open University and
OL,7,Folder schools programmes, there was
OL,8,Flittle in black and white by then apart
OL,9,Ffrom material which only the densest of
OL,10,Fviewers wouldn't realise was years old.
OL,11,
OL,12,FIt would be no shock to viewers much
OL,13,Fover the age of 6 or 7 ` even those
OL,14,Fwatching with a brand new colour set `
OL,15,Fto discover that an old film, Champion
OL,16,FThe Wonder Horse or Sergeant Bilko was
OL,17,Fin glorious monochrome.
OL,18,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13104
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G4/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES COut with the revolving cube
OL,4,Cand in with the cylinder
OL,5,
OL,6,FShortly after the change to the idents,
OL,7,FRadio Times stopped highlighting colour
OL,8,Fprogrammes too. Instead a weekly
OL,9,Ffootnote to the listings reminded
OL,10,Freaders that "all BBC TV programmes are
OL,11,Fin colour...unless otherwise
OL,12,Findicated."
OL,13,
OL,14,FOf course, the 'BBC Colour' tag stayed
OL,15,Fon end credits for another three years.
OL,16,FThe reason for this isn't so
OL,17,Fimmediately obvious.
OL,18,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
