OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES COut with the revolving cube
OL,4,Cand in with the cylinder
OL,5,
OL,6,FIntriguingly with the Presentation
OL,7,Frefresh, the BBC Two clock got a
OL,8,Fradical new look.
OL,9,
OL,10,FLittle is known about the new BBC Two
OL,11,Fclock although there is a
OL,12,Freconstruction of it online.
OL,13,
OL,14,FWhat we do know is that it was very
OL,15,Fquickly abandoned. The old clock
OL,16,Freturned. (Pedantic note ` we don't
OL,17,Fknow for sure when the line between the
OL,18,Fident and the clock was removed. Was
OL,19,Fthis before December 1974? Or when the
OL,20,Fold clock returned?)
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13106
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G6/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES COut with the revolving cube
OL,4,Cand in with the cylinder
OL,5,
OL,6,FA Kaleidoscope junction from early 1975
OL,7,Fshows the clock branded 'BBC2 COLOUR' `
OL,8,Fminus the line ` in use during
OL,9,Fafternoon adult education programmes
OL,10,Fbut the use of this version may have
OL,11,Fbeen an operational error. It is
OL,12,Fpresumed that two versions of the clock
OL,13,F` one without the suffix ` were always
OL,14,Favailable to the announcer.
OL,15,
OL,16,FQuite why the new clock failed is a
OL,17,Fmystery.
OL,18,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13107
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G7/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES COut with the revolving cube
OL,4,Cand in with the cylinder
OL,5,
OL,6,FIf someone disliked it intensely ` or
OL,7,Fif it proved impractical operationally
OL,8,F` why did this not get picked up
OL,9,Fbeforehand?
OL,10,
OL,11,FAnother thing worth mentioning is that
OL,12,Fthe corporate BBC Two logo remained a
OL,13,Fkey part of the channel's look with its
OL,14,Fprominent role on the clock.
OL,15,
OL,16,FWhy did it stay on the BBC Two clock
OL,17,Fwhen its BBC One counterpart was
OL,18,Fremoved from the globe, clock and
OL,19,Fschools diamond?
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13108
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G8/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES COut with the revolving cube
OL,4,Cand in with the cylinder
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe changes on BBC Two were less
OL,7,Fsignificant than the much-loved
OL,8,Fmodification to the globe.
OL,9,
OL,10,FAt this point in time, there were still
OL,11,Fviewers who could not receive BBC Two
OL,12,Fand others who rarely watched what to
OL,13,Fthem ` if not to those of us brought up
OL,14,Fon BBC TV B ` was the third channel
OL,15,Frather than the second.
OL,16,
OL,17,FIt would take another 16 years ` with
OL,18,Ftwo more revamps along the way ` for
OL,19,FBBC Two to finally gain a powerful
OL,20,Fvisual identity.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13109
SC,0009
